      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture. Let me write the improved version — the main issues are:\n1. A wall-of-code single-line call in `test_comparisons()` with 13 arguments\n2. Many unused data-provider methods and imports cluttering the class\n3. The helper method name `doTest_comparisons_UtcInstant` is opaque\n4. Several constants only exist to serve the unused methodsThe improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version improves understandability by: removing all unused data-provider methods and their dead imports/constants, renaming the opaque helper to `assertInstantsInStrictAscendingOrder`, adding a brief doc comment explaining the invariant it checks, and formatting the 13-argument call in `test_comparisons()` with one `UtcInstant` per line."
